{"assignees": null, "author_login": "gkorland", "body": "## Summary\n\nWhen a `CREATE` introduces more distinct attribute names than the graph's attribute-id space can hold, the Rust engine (`falkordb/falkordb:edge`) reports **success** and creates the node with **zero properties** \u2014 not just the overflowing ones, *all* of them. The C engine returns a clean error and creates nothing.\n\nFound while triaging #2331 against Rust. The security substance of #233", "closed_at": "2026-10-15T14:10:45Z", "container": "FalkorDB/FalkorDB", "created_at": "2026-08-17T07:20:15Z", "due_date": null, "key": null, "kind": "issue", "labels": ["bug", "rust"], "merged_at": null, "number": 2539, "priority": null, "source": "github", "state": "closed", "status_category": null, "title": "[Rust] Exceeding the attribute-id cap silently drops every property on the node and still reports success", "type": "WorkItem", "uid": "github:FalkorDB/FalkorDB:issue:2539", "updated_at": "2026-10-15T14:10:45Z", "url": "https://github.com/FalkorDB/FalkorDB/issues/2539"}
{"author_login": "gkorland", "body": "Re-verified independently. **Confirmed real, and the report is accurate.** Reproduced both engines' behaviour, including the incidental C crash.\n\n**Rust `edge`** \u2014 bisected the threshold on a fresh gr", "created_at": "2026-08-17T12:33:24Z", "source": "github", "type": "Comment", "uid": "github:FalkorDB/FalkorDB:comment:IC_kwDOJ9smgc8AAAABPN0EsQ", "url": "https://github.com/FalkorDB/FalkorDB/issues/2539#issuecomment-5316084913", "work_item_uid": "github:FalkorDB/FalkorDB:issue:2539"}
