{"assignees": null, "author_login": "flowt-au", "body": "Hi. \r\nI intend to implement FalkorDB as a replacement for RedisGraph as soon as I get through my current backlog! ;-) \r\n\r\nI know RedisGraph doesn't support nested json objects on graph nodes because Cypher doesn't support it (as I understand).\r\n\r\nI am in the process of working up a way to use RedisJson (which of course does support nested json) in conjunction with RedisGraph / FalkorDB. I am just ", "closed_at": null, "container": "FalkorDB/FalkorDB", "created_at": "2023-08-08T01:06:22Z", "due_date": null, "key": null, "kind": "issue", "labels": ["enhancement"], "merged_at": null, "number": 8, "priority": null, "source": "github", "state": "open", "status_category": null, "title": "Nested JSON on nodes?", "type": "WorkItem", "uid": "github:FalkorDB/FalkorDB:issue:8", "updated_at": "2026-08-03T21:52:24Z", "url": "https://github.com/FalkorDB/FalkorDB/issues/8"}
{"author_login": "swilly22", "body": "Hi @flowt-au thank you for opening an issue.\r\n\r\nIndeed the decision against allowing nested Map objects as attribute values was for compatibility reasons,\r\nbut let us reconsider, I'll update on our de", "created_at": "2023-08-09T07:37:58Z", "source": "github", "type": "Comment", "uid": "github:FalkorDB/FalkorDB:comment:IC_kwDOJ9smgc5jlsqy", "url": "https://github.com/FalkorDB/FalkorDB/issues/8#issuecomment-1670826674", "work_item_uid": "github:FalkorDB/FalkorDB:issue:8"}
{"author_login": "flowt-au", "body": "Thanks! I have coded up a solution that takes the nested objects (in my case a map of arrays) and for each key in the map makes a \"sub node\" of the node owning the map. It seems to be a good solution ", "created_at": "2023-08-09T07:52:30Z", "source": "github", "type": "Comment", "uid": "github:FalkorDB/FalkorDB:comment:IC_kwDOJ9smgc5jlxMP", "url": "https://github.com/FalkorDB/FalkorDB/issues/8#issuecomment-1670845199", "work_item_uid": "github:FalkorDB/FalkorDB:issue:8"}
{"author_login": "flowt-au", "body": "One other requirement I have that might be pushing the envelope way too far is that I need to be able to search the items in the nested map of arrays so I can get a list of nodes having specific items", "created_at": "2023-08-09T07:59:31Z", "source": "github", "type": "Comment", "uid": "github:FalkorDB/FalkorDB:comment:IC_kwDOJ9smgc5jlzhC", "url": "https://github.com/FalkorDB/FalkorDB/issues/8#issuecomment-1670854722", "work_item_uid": "github:FalkorDB/FalkorDB:issue:8"}
